[
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have something like this in mathlib / open PRs? I'm happy to start a simple PR if not.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">End</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Representation</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isIntegral_character</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FiniteDimensional</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Representation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsIntegral</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">character</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><del>I didn't use <code>FDRep</code> since it seems to force same unverse level between <code>k</code> and <code>G</code>?</del> Just noticed that <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39022\">#39022</a> fixed the universe issue.</p>",
        "id": 603655189,
        "sender_full_name": "Suzuka Yu",
        "timestamp": 1781599770
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(update) something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FDRep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsIntegral</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">character</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 603659523,
        "sender_full_name": "Suzuka Yu",
        "timestamp": 1781600619
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Proposes <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40665\">#40665</a></p>",
        "id": 603695008,
        "sender_full_name": "Suzuka Yu",
        "timestamp": 1781607785
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is <code>IsAlgClosed k</code> necessary? In general you can just base change <code>V</code> to the algebraic closure of <code>k</code> and the character is not changed?</p>",
        "id": 603717522,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1781612485
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why not prove the result for <code>Representation</code> first and deduce it for <code>FDRep</code>?</p>",
        "id": 603757103,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1781619251
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Good point! I've written the version without <code>IsAlgClosed k</code> and for <code>Representation</code>, <del>will upload it soon</del> uploaded. Thanks for the suggestions!</p>",
        "id": 603976948,
        "sender_full_name": "Suzuka Yu",
        "timestamp": 1781661390
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Humm, I noticed that in <code>Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Character</code>, we have namespace for <code>FDRep</code> before <code>Representation</code>. In that case should I prove the result for <code>FDRep</code> first?</p>",
        "id": 603983710,
        "sender_full_name": "Suzuka Yu",
        "timestamp": 1781663598
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/FDRep.html#FDRep.of\">FDRep.of</a> require <code>R</code> and <code>V</code> to be in the same universe, is there any mathematical reason behind this?</p>",
        "id": 604021544,
        "sender_full_name": "Suzuka Yu",
        "timestamp": 1781675243
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Representation theory has unfortunately various universe issues, and it's not clear how to solve all of them. Reasons include slowdowns and actual mathematical problems (is the category always monoidal, when we allow 3 universes?). It is also possible that in this specific case it's just an accident, you can try to make it more universes polymorphic and see what happens.</p>",
        "id": 604022179,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1781675446
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But also universe monomorphism isn't the end of the world. After all, most of mathematics fits inside <code>Type</code>!</p>",
        "id": 604024625,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1781676189
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The advantage of doing <code>Representation</code> first is that there are no universe issues. I would do <code>Representation</code> and then deduce for <code>FDRep</code> and if someone cares enough to solve the universe issues later then your work will be easy to upgrade.</p>",
        "id": 604039396,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1781680036
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks! My naive attack on the universe issue doesn't work well so yes I'll just do <code>Representation</code> first.</p>",
        "id": 604067557,
        "sender_full_name": "Suzuka Yu",
        "timestamp": 1781685712
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"130384\">Riccardo Brasca</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Integrality.20of.20character/near/604022179\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Representation theory has unfortunately various universe issues, and it's not clear how to solve all of them. Reasons include slowdowns and actual mathematical problems (is the category always monoidal, when we allow 3 universes?). It is also possible that in this specific case it's just an accident, you can try to make it more universes polymorphic and see what happens.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><code>max {u, v}</code> is one of the solution but I don't recommend it</p>",
        "id": 604096600,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1781691432
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>Rep</code> is now less cursed as long as we keep ourselves away from tensor product</p>",
        "id": 604096715,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1781691457
    }
